export anchor TattooFlashStyle:
    number: 154
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Tattoo flash
    idea: A traditional tattoo flash sheet on warm paper, where every project is a bold outlined design with a ribbon banner, numbers sit in arched badges and swallows, stars and daggers carry the meaning.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #f3e9d2, the page behind the sheet
        sheet: #fbf5e6, panels, badges, the header and the greeting banner
        ink: #141210, all text and every heavy outline
        flashRed: #a8201a, the primary button, ribbons, this week bars, the overdue badge and Behind
        leafGreen: #2b5e33, ribbons and the On track word
        sailorBlue: #1d4470, ribbons, swallows and eye motifs
        mustard: #e3b23c, stars, meter stripes, banner tails and the focus halo, never text
        tobacco: #5a4632, notes, team names, times and the At risk word
        skin: #efc9a4, the avatar disc only
    type:
        Three stacks. Labels, numbers and titles use Rockwell, Clarendon,
        Roboto Slab, Courier New, Georgia, serif in heavy weights, mostly
        uppercase. The greeting uses Brush Script MT, Segoe Script, Snell
        Roundhand, cursive at 46px. Body uses Georgia, Times New Roman,
        serif at 17px with 1.5 line height. Badge numbers are 58px 900,
        section titles 26px caps, ribbon names 15px caps, labels 13 to
        14px caps tracked 0.06 to 0.2em.
    layout:
        A boxed header with a swallow and red outlined brand, centred
        outlined nav chips with a star on Home, then search, New project,
        a round bell with a red count and the avatar. The greeting is
        centred, a spaced caps date above a script line set inside an
        outlined banner with mustard tails and a swallow on each side,
        then an outlined box with a crossed square saying 4 tasks are
        overdue. Four badges with arched tops hold the numbers, each with
        a black caps label strip, the overdue badge filled red. Below, a
        two to one grid. The projects panel is a dotted flash sheet of
        six cards in three columns, each with a flash motif drawing such
        as a rose, ship, eye, anchor, swallow or banded heart, a red,
        green or blue ribbon with forked tails carrying the name, the team
        in italic, a striped pill meter, the facts line and a status chip.
        The side column holds the activity list with a swallow before each
        row and dashed dividers, then the chart panel with outlined bars,
        cream for last week and red for this week. Below 980px the grid
        stacks and cards drop to two columns, then one below 440px.
    spacing: A 4px base in steps of 8, 12, 16, 24 and 32. The sheet has a 24px gutter and 20px panel padding.
    density: Medium. Each design is a self-contained motif with name, team, meter, facts and status.
    corners: Small 3 to 8px radii. Badges have arched tops. Ribbons have forked tails.
    borders: Heavy ink outlines, 4px on panels and badges, 3px on cards and buttons, 2px on chips, nav and fields.
    shadows: Only a hard 3px ink offset under buttons. Panels carry a faint 12px dot stipple.
    icons:
        Flash motifs with thick ink outlines and flat fills. A filled star
        means On track, a dagger means At risk, a red box with a white
        cross means Behind and overdue, and swallows mark activity rows.
    focus: A 3px ink outline offset 3px inside a 7px mustard halo.
    tone: Warm and proud, with short caps labels and a script greeting, such as Latest work and six designs on the sheet.
